src/physical-scene.ts is copied from Cubistry packages/cube-viewer/src/physical-scene.ts,
revision efafcc1d97687eccea0cde87a230f447ce1b6c66, source SHA-256
73c9882b48c107b43513600e3dafbf1c2f9be1b1b44b30fcc1c2ebaf29c7c79f.
Imports use existing local render-only helpers; piece and sticker identifiers use
opaque strings instead of numbers, and Construction is a local type. The source
scene is staged for integration; the existing production entry point is unchanged.
The staged physical scene additionally accepts explicit opaque body poses for pieces
without sticker frames, rejects overlapping identities, and validates required poses
before synchronization. These extensions do not define or mutate puzzle state.
The source turn method also accepts a unit axis vector and an explicit pivot; the
original numeric axis form remains available. This is a renderer-only extension.
The scene exposes validated direct Core-owned presentation poses for all bodies;
this preserves arbitrary body quaternions without turning them into puzzle state.
The source SmartRotation controller additionally supports adopting a validated
snapshot without replacing the instance held by the source input binding.
The stage uses the source binding as its sole input path; the native stylesheet
is copied into the distributed viewer output.

